
# Probe for the service.publish reversal (join-c plan Task 2, Step 3): "has
# this service description already been deleted?" service.publish carries
# no forward probe (Plan A Task 5 classified it (b), 409-safe) -- this one
# exists purely for the reversal direction.
#
# CONFIRMED LIVE (apps/join-api/tests/fixtures/xroad/
# unjoin.service_delete.probe.json, docs/xroad-770-notes.md #11): GET
# /clients/{id}/service-descriptions always 200s -- absence of the deleted
# description is an EMPTY LIST, not a 404 (one of the two probes in this
# task that does NOT signal absence with a 404 -- do not assume it does).
# The (future) executor decides from the raw body whether
# @CAP_P@_@SC@_description_id is still present.
GET https://{{@HOSTVAR@}}:4000/api/v1/clients/{{@CAP_P@_client_id}}/service-descriptions
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{@SESS_P@_xsrf_token}}

HTTP 200

[Captures]
@CAP_P@_service_descriptions: body
